#### How telnet communicate with QEMU?

1) Map a QEMU uart to tcp port, and connect telnet to the QEMU port.
```
-serial tcp:127.0.0.1:1124,server
```

2) Input a char 'x' into telnet, you must press "enter" to commit the input.
The actual input sequence sent to server is 'x\r\n'.

3) telnet itself will display the char sequence 'x\r\n' BEFORE receiving echo back
from the QEMU uart.

4) QEMU echo back the sequence 'x\r\n'.

5) telnet display the newly received sequence 'x\r\n'.


